{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe `Verify Authorship Identity` CI gate (`.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`) fails closed\nwhen the blobless CI-checkout pack of the `tickets` branch exceeds\n`REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` (today `102400` = 100 MiB, a deliberate growth canary from commit\n`16a1a385` / ticket `037b`). The pack is currently ~481 MiB, so the gate is RED (bug\n`defensive-buckskin-rhino` / `a453-193b-2864-451b`).\n\nThe proof on parent epic `536b-8930-b922-4063` establishes that the ONLY lever that shrinks this\nblobless pack is reducing reachable commit+tree objects via causal-stability history collapse, and\nthat even maximal SAFE coalescing (N=30d horizon) lands at ~365-380 MiB — it cannot reach 100 MiB\nwithout an unsafe <4-day horizon. Therefore a temporary budget-raise bridge is unavoidable to get\nthe health lane green while the reclaim mechanism + structural fixes (W1 batch write lane, W2 root\ntree shard) land.\n\n## Scope of THIS ticket (the bridge, this change only)\n\nRaise `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` from `102400` (100 MiB) to `563200` (550 MiB) — ~70 MiB\nheadroom over today's 481 MiB pack — and add a self-documenting comment immediately above the\nvalue that names the restore ticket (`fluorspar-comparable-zeren` / `0894-b9b8-6590-4904`) so the\nbridge is reversible and traceable. This is a temporary, deliberately-reversible loosening of the\ncanary, NOT a permanent budget change; the restore is tracked separately.\n\nOne companion test is coupled to the declared budget:\n`tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py::test_pack_guard_contract` reads the live\nworkflow env and asserts it equals the parametrized value, so that expectation must move in\nlockstep (`102400` -> `563200`). The other `102400`/`_STANDALONE_LIMIT` occurrences in the test\nsuite are subprocess-env fixtures passed as explicit guard overrides (not read from the workflow),\nso they are unaffected and stay as-is.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe history-reclaim mechanism (S0-S3), W1/W2 structural fixes, and the eventual restore to 100 MiB\nare separate tickets under the epic. This ticket does no history rewrite and no prod mutation of\nthe `tickets` branch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` in `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml` is set to `563200`.\n- [ ] A comment immediately above the value marks it as a TEMPORARY bridge and names restore ticket `fluorspar-comparable-zeren` (`0894-b9b8-6590-4904`).\n- [ ] The companion coupled expectation is updated: `test_pack_guard_contract` in `tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py` moves its parametrized limit from `102400` to `563200` so it re-asserts the new declared budget.\n- [ ] The guard control flow is unchanged: only the threshold value, its self-documenting comment, and that one coupled test expectation change; the `git count-objects` fail-closed logic is untouched.\n- [ ] The commit carries a `rebar-ticket:` trailer for this ticket and a DCO sign-off.\n- [ ] The change is pushed to Gerrit for review (`LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`) and is NOT self-submitted.\n\n## Portability\n\n`REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` is a plain workflow environment variable consumed by a POSIX\n`bash`/`git count-objects` guard; changing its value introduces no dependence on any single CI\nprovider and no new capability. The `project.portability` criterion is satisfied because the guard\nremains a provider-agnostic shell check whose only input is a git object count."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788045274720071707,"uuid":"5d91e512-1e9a-4d99-95e1-d94e79adf05a"}